 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )((3-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )+10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +3)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7$, we have that the only real eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-3$ (both with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3399fe8e-8176-5e35-93d5-9a34329ea9c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186272116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442274 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442274 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442274 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442275 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442275 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442275 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442276 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186